  "review_notes": [
    "Reviewed the current top-level proposal.json through line 243, functionality.md through line 34, fact-dispositions.json through line 445, and link-dispositions.json through line 245. The verdict concerns this exact proposal, not the earlier librarian proposal embedded in context.",
    "All eight proposed writes address owned subjects and are supported by canonical source and inspected foreign producers, consumers, and callback bindings. No entities, merges, new links, or follow-up mutations are proposed.",
    "The proposal correctly distinguishes entry-time storage of the calculated rate from its later consumption by the Rebound transition. Only the entry-time calculation is established to precede the observed transient-damage reset.",
    "The additional ReboundStop_Anim state-behavior write consistently corrects frame-zero wording to anim_start=0 API semantics. Fighter_ChangeMotionState initially stores start minus rate, and zero blend may select animation metadata rather than effective no blending.",
    "The attack-clash mapping is supported by fighter/fighter and item/fighter hitcapsule producers and the guarded engine entry. Surface-rebound links are appropriately rejected rather than justified from the Rebound name.",
    "Boundary review confirms conditional rather than unconditional physics suppression, strict friction comparisons, unchecked entry arithmetic, parts-based animation completion, guarded completion destinations, and the literal GA_Ground collision-result comparison. Physical collision-result polarity and target exceptional-float behavior remain deferred.",
    "Retained ownership language is accepted only as Fighter association through user_data; exclusive ownership, compiled layout, and arbitrary callback destruction/reentrancy safety are expressly not established. These are specific deferrals, not additional proved claims."
  ],
